From 819b81a75c9eb687055fef83d6be72f6198667ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ShorterKing <automobilehacks@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 19:10:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] staging: prima: avoid oops on external USB WiFi disconnect

The __hdd_netdev_notifier_call() notifier is invoked for all
net_device instances, not only those owned by the prima driver.

Existing checks rely on interface naming ("wlan"/"p2p") and
ieee80211_ptr, which allows unrelated devices such as USB WiFi
adapters (e.g. mt7601u) to pass validation. This results in
netdev_priv being incorrectly interpreted as a prima
hdd_adapter_t.

During device disconnect, the net_device private data may already
be freed (LIST_POISON), leading to a kernel oops when accessed:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address dead...
  pc : hdd_netdev_notifier_call+0x70/0x154

Fix this by validating the adapter magic before dereferencing.
If the magic does not match WLAN_HDD_ADAPTER_MAGIC, ignore the
device.

This prevents invalid access to foreign net_device instances and
avoids crashes on USB WiFi disconnect.

Signed-off-by: ShorterKing <automobilehacks@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_main.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_main.c b/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
index 751178285..4fbf1fca2 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
@@ -357,6 +357,20 @@ static int __hdd_netdev_notifier_call(struct notifier_block * nb,
       return NOTIFY_DONE;
    }
 
+   /* Verify this net_device actually belongs to prima.
+    * Other drivers (e.g. mt7601u) also name their interfaces "wlan*" and
+    * set ieee80211_ptr, so they pass the guards above. Their netdev_priv
+    * is not a prima hdd_adapter_t and must not be dereferenced as one.
+    * On disconnect the private data may already be freed (LIST_POISON),
+    * causing a kernel oops at the pHddCtx dereference below.
+    */
+   if (pAdapter->magic != WLAN_HDD_ADAPTER_MAGIC)
+   {
+      hddLog(VOS_TRACE_LEVEL_INFO,"%s: magic mismatch, ignoring non-prima dev %s",
+             __func__, dev->name);
+      return NOTIFY_DONE;
+   }
+
    pHddCtx = WLAN_HDD_GET_CTX(pAdapter);
    if (NULL == pHddCtx)
    {
